Assignment 3 – Terminal Navigation Practice Sheet

Objective

To learn basic terminal commands used for folder navigation, file management, and web development.

1. Basic Terminal Commands

No.| Task| macOS / Linux / Git Bash| PowerShell
1| Show current folder| "pwd"| "pwd"
2| List files| "ls"| "ls"
3| Show hidden files and details| "ls -la"| "ls -Force"
4| Create a folder| "mkdir practice"| "mkdir practice"
5| Enter a folder| "cd practice"| "cd practice"
6| Create an empty file| "touch index.html"| "ni index.html"
7| Create nested folders| "mkdir -p css/images"| "mkdir css/images"
8| Go up one level| "cd .."| "cd .."
9| Go to home directory| "cd ~"| "cd ~"
10| Copy a file| "cp index.html backup.html"| "cp index.html backup.html"
11| Rename or move a file| "mv backup.html old.html"| "mv backup.html old.html"
12| Delete a file| "rm old.html"| "rm old.html"
13| Delete a folder| "rm -r css"| "rm -r css"
14| Display file contents| "cat index.html"| "cat index.html"
15| Clear the terminal| "clear"| "cls"
16| Open folder in VS Code| "code ."| "code ."

2. Practice Exercise

Task: Starting from the home directory, create a website folder containing "index.html", "css/style.css", and an "images" folder.

Commands Used

Step 1: Go to the home directory

cd ~

Step 2: Create the folders

mkdir -p website/css website/images

Step 3: Create the files

touch website/index.html website/css/style.css

Step 4: Enter the CSS folder

cd website/css

Step 5: Return to the website folder

cd ..

Step 6: List all files and folders recursively

ls -R

Step 7: Rename index.html to home.html

mv index.html home.html

Step 8: Rename home.html back to index.html

mv home.html index.html

Step 9: Open the folder in VS Code

code .

3. Expected Folder Structure

website/
├── index.html
├── css/
│   └── style.css
└── images/

Conclusion

This practice sheet covers essential terminal commands for navigating directories, creating files and folders, copying, renaming, deleting, and opening a web development project in VS Code.